 work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Tag Questions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use tag questions to ask for clarification and confirmation.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Tag questions are short questions that are added at the end of statements.<br>You mostly use tag questions in spoken English when you want to:<ul><li><span class=\"strong\">clarify/confirm whether something is true or not true</span>, or</li><li><span class=\"strong\">to encourage a response</span> from someone you are talking to.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ol><li value=\"1\">An <span class=\"strong\">affirmative</span> statement is followed by a <span class=\"strong\">negative</span> question tag.<br/> Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying 'yes' <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>You <span class=\"strong\">were</span> taken by surprise, <span class=\"strong\">weren't you?</span></li> <li>You <span class=\"strong\">are</span> Canadian, <span class=\"strong\">aren't</span> you?</li> <li>She <span class=\"strong\">has</span> a brother, <span class=\"strong\">doesn't</span> she?</li> <li>He <span class=\"strong\">can</span> speak English, <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> he?</li></ul></span></li></ol>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ol><li value=\"2\">A <span class=\"strong\">negative</span> statement is followed by an <span class=\"strong\">affirmative</span> question tag.<br/> Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying 'no'  <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>You <span class=\"strong\">weren't</span> taken by surprise, <span class=\"strong\">were you? </span></li> <li>You <span class=\"strong\">aren't</span> Canadian, <span class=\"strong\">are</span> you?</li> <li>She <span class=\"strong\">doesn't</span> have a brother, <span class=\"strong\">does</span> she?</li> <li>He <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> speak English, <span class=\"strong\">can</span> he?</li></ul></span> </li></ol>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If the main verb is <span class=\"italic\">to be</span> or a <span class=\"strong\">modal verb</span>, the tag will be the same. <br/>For <span class=\"strong\">all other main verbs</span>, use the tag <span class=\"italic\">do</span>/<span class=\"italic\">does </span>or <span class=\"italic\">did</span>/<span class=\"italic\">didn't</span>. <br/>Look at the examples in the chart.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":11,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Main Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tag\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Main Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tag\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" He is/was\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"isn't/wasn't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" She has/had\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"doesn't/didn't she?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You are\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"aren't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"don't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" He can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"can't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" He likes\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"doesn't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" We could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"couldn't we?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You like\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"don't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"won't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You liked\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"didn't you?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "It never is easy when the money runs out, is it?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It sounds like a daunting task, doesn't it?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "All of this won't help, will it? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I can do this, can't I?  ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Future Tense vs. The Future Perfect Tense ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Future tense (<span class=\"italic\">will</span>) to talk about a one-time action or event that will happen in the future.<br/>You use the Future Perfect tense to talk about a future action that will be completed before another action in the future. This tense is used to clarify the order of events that will occur in the future. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The Future Perfect tense is similar to the Present Perfect tense, but your perspective is in the future instead if the present.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">I will arrive at work at 7:45 a.m. We can start the meeting at 8:00 a.m. I <span class=\"strong\">will have arrived</span> at the office by 8:00.<br/>The plane will take off at 9:00 a.m. You will arrive at the airport at 9:15 a.m. When you arrive, the plane <span class=\"strong\">will have taken off</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the chart for the structure of the Future Perfect tense:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">will</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(<span class=\\\"italic\\\">not</span>) <span class=\\\"italic\\\">have </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"found\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"created\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"not have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"searched\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": " *Notice the position of <span class=\"italic\">not</span>. It comes between <span class=\"italic\">will </span>and <span class=\"italic\">have</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In my first month, I will have found my big problem that I am going to solve. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I will have identified a field that I am interested in and I will have explored work opportunities in that area.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "In month two, I will have made a list of companies that are trying to solve my problem and hopefully, share my interests. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I will have researched each company and combed their web pages for job listings.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Then, in my third month, I will have searched my circle of friends to see who is connected to my target companies.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Finally in month four, I will have created a resume that is innovative and will capture people's attention. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "In the resume, I will have highlighted how my passion can help the company meet its aspirations. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Create and fill out a standard job application form online; name, age, address, phone number, previous job, and why you want to work for the company.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Swap the forms with another partner and role-play.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "One partner will be the boss asking for clarification and an opinion using tag questions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The other partner will be the applicant and correct his/her information.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Switch roles.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Afterwards, try and add more complex categories to the application form and role-play again.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I use tag questions to clarify information.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write an application form inquiring about information.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I perform a role-play using the target grammar, tag questions.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to tighten your belt", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to try to save money by buying less", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I will need to tighten my belt.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to look for work.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to comb", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to arrange", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I will have researched each company and combed their web pages for job listings.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "daunting ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "causing fear or doubt in one's abilities", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It sounds like a daunting task, doesn't it?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "nonetheless", "type": "name"}, {"content": "however", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Nonetheless, establishing contacts already in the company is a great way to discover more about the organization.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "innovative", "type": "name"}, {"content": "new; original", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I will have created a resume that is innovative and will capture people's attention. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "aspirations", "type": "name"}, {"content": "ambitions", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I will have highlighted how my passion can help the company meet its aspirations. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "circle of friends", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a group of close friends", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I will have searched my circle of friends to see who is connected to my target companies. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob03aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}], "type": "sena"}